  "solution": {
    "text": "Family has four children in total.<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Total number of ways in which at least two girls are there</p><p>is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></math></p><p>Favourable case in which all are girls is <math><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
